course: dictionary
lesson: 471
title: Many meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is right. Arrest is one of them. «Jokes about bombs or weapons at an airport are treated as real threats, and people can be arrested for them.» Here arrested means the police take someone away because they may have broken the law.
explain: Arrest can also mean to stop something. The word «arresting» in «arresting the spread of a disease» means stopping the disease from spreading. Cardiac arrest is a different kind of arrest: the heart suddenly stops pumping properly, and that is an emergency.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. If «stop» fits the sentence and makes sense, you have found the right meaning. If you are still not sure, read the words around the word again, or use a dictionary.
fact: To arrest someone means the police take them away because they may have broken the law.
fact: An arrest is the noun: it is when the police do this.
fact: To arrest something can mean to stop it, as in arresting the spread of a disease.
fact: Cardiac arrest is when the heart suddenly stops pumping properly. It is an emergency: call for help and use CPR and a defibrillator.
fact: Real police never ask for payment by message or phone. «Pay or be arrested» messages are scare scams.
exercise: «Jokes about bombs or weapons at an airport are treated as real threats, and people can be arrested for them.» What does arrested mean here? | *Taken away by the police because they may have broken the law | Given a prize for being funny | Let go with a friendly warning | Stopped from talking for a minute
exercise: Cardiac arrest is when the heart does what? | Fills up with happy feelings | Beats very fast when you run | *Suddenly stops pumping properly | Gets a new colour
exercise: Which word could replace arresting in «arresting the spread of a disease»? | starting | *stopping | painting | counting
test: The police made an arrest after the bank robbery. What does arrest mean here? | The police gave a prize to the bank | The police stopped the bank from opening | *The police took a person away because they may have broken the law | The police painted the bank door
test: Someone near you has cardiac arrest. What should you do first? | *Call for help | Ask them to run around | Go home and have a sleep | Wait and see if their heart starts on its own
exam: Mia says arrest always means the police take someone away. Is she right? | Yes, arrest always means the same thing and has no other meaning | No, arrest means to dance | Yes, but only in stories | *No, arrest can also mean to stop something, as in arresting the spread of a disease
